00:26:10,703 --> 00:26:11,905
- [Woman Narrator] Next,
you'll be escorted by a guide

764
00:26:11,905 --> 00:26:14,573
past the door of
the round building,

765
00:26:14,573 --> 00:26:17,477
the entranceway to America.

766
00:26:17,477 --> 00:26:21,313
This is the ultimate
answer, the ideal.

767
00:26:21,313 --> 00:26:22,482
This is what you've all--

768
00:26:22,482 --> 00:26:24,217
- [Mike] The cast of "Godspell."

769
00:26:24,217 --> 00:26:26,820
- [Woman Narrator] America,
the land of beauty,

770
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:29,655
where all your dreams
will come true.

771
00:26:29,655 --> 00:26:30,490
- [Mike] America.

772
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:31,758
- [Tom] Oh, America.

773
00:26:31,758 --> 00:26:33,158
- [Woman Narrator] You
have all been trained.

774
00:26:33,158 --> 00:26:34,693
America,

775
00:26:34,693 --> 00:26:38,632
the happiness of your new world
forever, forever, forever!

776
00:26:38,632 --> 00:26:40,433
- [Tom] Oh, they blew their
budget on the echo chamber.

777
00:26:40,433 --> 00:26:41,735
(applauding)

778
00:26:41,735 --> 00:26:43,970
- [Crow] America not
available in some areas.

779
00:26:43,970 --> 00:26:46,072
(applauding)

780
00:26:46,072 --> 00:26:47,307
- [Mike] Thank you,

781
00:26:47,307 --> 00:26:49,008
we'll now begin the
Aunt Clara symposium.

782
00:26:49,008 --> 00:26:50,510
- Does anyone have
any questions?

783
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:52,912
- [Tom] Yeah, are you
and Dick York friends?

784
00:26:52,912 --> 00:26:53,747
- Yes, Richard?

785
00:26:55,548 --> 00:26:58,250
- Dr. Jameson, I
found something today

786
00:26:58,250 --> 00:27:00,487
that I think might
be from America.

787
00:27:00,487 --> 00:27:02,522
It was floating in the river.

788
00:27:02,522 --> 00:27:03,457
- What is it?

789
00:27:03,457 --> 00:27:04,690
- [Crow] It's a Gambino, sir.

790
00:27:05,858 --> 00:27:07,393
- [Mike] Future
anchorman, there.

791
00:27:09,228 --> 00:27:11,965
- [Tom] We chipped in
and got you this beer.

792
00:27:11,965 --> 00:27:13,967
- This is not from America.

793
00:27:13,967 --> 00:27:15,435
It comes from the river.

794
00:27:15,435 --> 00:27:17,903
- [Crow] What, where you cloned
from a sack of doorknobs?

795
00:27:17,903 --> 00:27:20,173
- I'll just keep
it for the museum.

796
00:27:20,173 --> 00:27:21,640
- But it's mine.

797
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:22,808
- [Mike] You wanna watch "Sonny
& Cher" tonight, young man?

798
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:25,978
- Richard, this
belongs to all of us.

799
00:27:25,978 --> 00:27:27,580
- [Tom] Dick Sargent, Communist.

800
00:27:27,580 --> 00:27:28,415
- [Mike] Oooh.

801
00:27:28,415 --> 00:27:30,017
- Well, that's it.

802
00:27:30,017 --> 00:27:31,383
Good afternoon, all.

803
00:27:31,383 --> 00:27:33,052
If you have any
further questions,

804
00:27:33,052 --> 00:27:34,787
please go to the confessional.

805
00:27:34,787 --> 00:27:36,690
(audience applauding)

806
00:27:36,690 --> 00:27:38,625
- [Crow] Stop that
man, he has my can!

807
00:27:41,928 --> 00:27:44,830
- [Mike] Dick Sargent
is the Bionic Woman.

808
00:27:44,830 --> 00:27:47,067
- Find out how this got
through the water valves

809
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:49,735
and who the hell was
in charge of cleanup?

810
00:27:49,735 --> 00:27:51,037
I want them out of here!

811
00:27:51,037 --> 00:27:52,305
- [Crow] Mr. York?

812
00:27:52,305 --> 00:27:54,407
- [Mike] Mr. York, will
you sign this, Mr. York?

813
00:27:56,810 --> 00:27:59,278
- [Crow] Line up to hear
Firefall's latest hit.

814
00:28:00,813 --> 00:28:03,417
(somber music)

815
00:28:08,522 --> 00:28:09,888
- [Female Voice]
How may we help you?

816
00:28:09,888 --> 00:28:11,090
- I have a question.

817
00:28:11,090 --> 00:28:12,692
- [Mike] I'll hang
up and listen.

818
00:28:12,692 --> 00:28:17,563
- What does
M-I-L-W-A-U-K-E-E spell?

819
00:28:17,563 --> 00:28:18,498
- [Female Voice] Please wait.

820
00:28:18,498 --> 00:28:20,467
- [Tom] It spells $2.99 a case.

821
00:28:22,202 --> 00:28:25,172
- [Female Voice]
M-I-L-W-A-U-K-E-E

822
00:28:25,172 --> 00:28:27,640
appears to be some sort
of nonsense spelling.

823
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:30,543
- [Mike] Oh, it's Microsoft
Spell Check by Phone.

824
00:28:30,543 --> 00:28:33,212
- Dr. Jameson told me it
could be found in the river.

825
00:28:34,413 --> 00:28:35,648
- [Female Voiceover]
One moment, please.

826
00:28:35,648 --> 00:28:38,117
- [Tom] Dr. Jameson
is a big, dumb phony.

827
00:28:38,117 --> 00:28:39,618
- [Female Voiceover] There
is a rare kind of mineral

828
00:28:39,618 --> 00:28:41,988
that is called "Milwaukee."

829
00:28:41,988 --> 00:28:45,092
It can only be found in
certain parts of the river.

830
00:28:45,092 --> 00:28:46,625
- [Mike] Uh, do you buy that?

831
00:28:46,625 --> 00:28:48,762
- Can it be found in America?

832
00:28:48,762 --> 00:28:50,897
- [Female Voice] No, it can not.

833
00:28:50,897 --> 00:28:52,765
Is there anything else?

834
00:28:52,765 --> 00:28:54,167
- [Crow] Charles Van Dorken.

835
00:28:55,502 --> 00:28:58,303
- [Tom] They need better
funding for their language lab.

836
00:28:58,303 --> 00:29:00,473
- [Female Voice] I'm
glad we could help you.

837
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:04,110
(Crow chuckling)

838
00:29:04,110 --> 00:29:07,713
- [Crow] You'd get better
exercise sitting on a couch.

839
00:29:07,713 --> 00:29:09,815
- [Mike] Daddy, Rex
Tree, the Lumpy Man!

840
00:29:09,815 --> 00:29:11,952
(Crow and Tom laughing)

841
00:29:11,952 --> 00:29:13,185
- [Crow] The "go
as slow as you can

842
00:29:13,185 --> 00:29:14,953
"without tipping over" race.

843
00:29:14,953 --> 00:29:17,090
(Tom giggling)

844
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:19,858
(pleasant music)

845
00:29:20,727 --> 00:29:22,028
- [Mike] A separate piece...

846
00:29:22,028 --> 00:29:22,995
Of crap!

847
00:29:22,995 --> 00:29:24,730
(Tom laughing)

848
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:25,832
- [Tom] Oh hi, Richard!

849
00:29:25,832 --> 00:29:26,665
- [Crow] Hey, Richard!

850
00:29:26,665 --> 00:29:27,600
- [Mike] Hi, Richard!

851
00:29:29,668 --> 00:29:31,037
- [Tom] The rare tree dork.

852
00:29:34,040 --> 00:29:35,675
- [Crow] Thanks
for the subpoena.

853
00:29:37,010 --> 00:29:38,978
- [Mike] "Parts: The
Visible Panty Line Horror."

854
00:29:38,978 --> 00:29:39,978
- [Tom] Ugh.

855
00:29:41,413 --> 00:29:43,448
- [Crow] The clone yards
of Ernest and Julio Gallo.

856
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:46,385
- [Mike] We're
done picking dirt.

857
00:29:47,687 --> 00:29:50,022
- [Tom] I guess Bing
Crosby was selling hats.

858
00:29:52,292 --> 00:29:56,128
- [Crow] It says, "Please
help me down from this tree."

859
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:57,997
- [Tom] Oh, a lock
of his back hair.

860
00:30:00,667 --> 00:30:02,335
- [Mike] "Would you like
to share a quarter can

861
00:30:02,335 --> 00:30:04,337
"of water Old Mill with me?"

862
00:30:05,205 --> 00:30:08,708
(birds chirping)

863
00:30:08,708 --> 00:30:11,543
- [Tom] Oh, it's the refund
for my nose job, good.

864
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:12,845
- [Crow] Tome Jones, here.

865
00:30:15,848 --> 00:30:18,818
- [Mike] Okay, people,
time to harvest more ticks.

866
00:30:18,818 --> 00:30:19,985
(whistle blowing)

867
00:30:19,985 --> 00:30:21,888
- [Tom] Bozo Circus
is on the air!

868
00:30:21,888 --> 00:30:23,857
(singing circus tune)

869
00:30:23,857 --> 00:30:25,558
- [Lena] Hello, I'm Lena.

870
00:30:25,558 --> 00:30:26,825
- [Richard] I'm Richard.

871
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:27,893
- [Crow] I'm Richard,
I gotta remember that.

872
00:30:27,893 --> 00:30:29,562
I'm so bad with names.

873
00:30:29,562 --> 00:30:33,132
(crickets chirping)

874
00:30:33,132 --> 00:30:36,568
- [Mike] The scene was lit by
an Indiglo watch apparently.

875
00:30:37,903 --> 00:30:38,872
- Hey.

876
00:30:38,872 --> 00:30:39,838
- [Tom] Kiss me, you feeb.

877
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:41,107
- Why did you ask me here?

878
00:30:41,107 --> 00:30:42,608
- Because I wanted
to talk to you.

879
00:30:42,608 --> 00:30:44,310
From the first day we met,

880
00:30:44,310 --> 00:30:46,678
I knew there was something
different about you.

881
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:47,513
- [Mike Deep Voice] There is?

882
00:30:47,513 --> 00:30:48,582
- You know what it is?

883
00:30:48,582 --> 00:30:49,715
Your eyes.

884
00:30:49,715 --> 00:30:50,950
They're so alive.

885
00:30:50,950 --> 00:30:52,818
- [Crow] Your
nose, so truncated.

886
00:30:52,818 --> 00:30:54,387
- You know, I noticed
the difference too.

887
00:30:54,387 --> 00:30:55,655
I mean, you're not
like my friends.

888
00:30:55,655 --> 00:30:56,788
- [Tom] You're more icky.

889
00:30:56,788 --> 00:30:58,490
- Yours like mine, Richard.

890
00:30:58,490 --> 00:30:59,758
Why?

891
00:30:59,758 --> 00:31:01,860
- I don't know, Lena, I
asked the confessional

892
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:04,430
and it just said that it
was all part of the plan.

893
00:31:04,430 --> 00:31:05,898
- [Mike] Like Dan
Fogelberg said.

894
00:31:05,898 --> 00:31:06,865
- Yeah, me too.

895
00:31:08,367 --> 00:31:09,235
- Hey.

896
00:31:09,235 --> 00:31:10,168
- What?

897
00:31:10,168 --> 00:31:11,337
- It's getting a little cold.

898
00:31:11,337 --> 00:31:13,238
How about some
firewood and a fire?

899
00:31:13,238 --> 00:31:15,040
- [Crow] Mmm, she burns good.

900
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,342
- [Richard] How long
before you leave?

901
00:31:16,342 --> 00:31:17,577
- [Tom] Later on.

902
00:31:17,577 --> 00:31:19,078
- For America?

903
00:31:19,078 --> 00:31:19,912
Oh, I don't know.

904
00:31:20,813 --> 00:31:22,082
- [Mike] Watch your head there.

905
00:31:22,082 --> 00:31:23,917
- We go when it's time
and when we're ready.

906
00:31:23,917 --> 00:31:25,318
- Yeah, that's
what they tell us.

907
00:31:25,318 --> 00:31:26,152
Constantly.

908
00:31:27,587 --> 00:31:29,222
Where do you work, Lena?

909
00:31:29,222 --> 00:31:30,990
- I work in the (muffled word).

910
00:31:30,990 --> 00:31:32,225
- Huh?
- Oh, I like it, it's nice.

911
00:31:32,225 --> 00:31:33,325
- [Mike] I like the
(gibberish word).

912
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:35,127
- Gives me time to write.

913
00:31:35,127 --> 00:31:36,462
- Write?

914
00:31:36,462 --> 00:31:38,230
- Yeah, I write my
thoughts and my ideas.

915
00:31:38,230 --> 00:31:39,465
- [Crow] I've already
filled a Post-it note.

916
00:31:39,465 --> 00:31:41,300
- It was my special
place for writing.

917
00:31:42,335 --> 00:31:43,302
- It was?

918
00:31:43,302 --> 00:31:44,437
- [Tom] I'm not listening.

919
00:31:46,505 --> 00:31:47,540
- What's wrong?

920
00:31:47,540 --> 00:31:49,042
- Nothing's wrong.

921
00:31:49,042 --> 00:31:50,710
- Oh, come on, Lena, don't
be like everyone else.

922
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:52,312
You can tell me what's wrong.
- Big slab.

923
00:31:52,312 --> 00:31:54,747
- Richard, we are not supposed
to be talking like this.

924
00:31:54,747 --> 00:31:57,183
They told me it
was not important.

925
00:31:57,183 --> 00:31:58,785
- What's not important?

926
00:31:58,785 --> 00:32:00,320
- [Crow] My gosh you're ugly.

927
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:03,055
- His name was Allan

928
00:32:04,257 --> 00:32:06,458
and we met in compound
four when we were 16.

929
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:08,127
- [Mike] When I had a nose.

930
00:32:08,127 --> 00:32:09,395
- You know, he's
beautiful, Richard.

931
00:32:09,395 --> 00:32:11,030
- [Tom] Not like you.

932
00:32:11,030 --> 00:32:13,132
- His hair was like the
sun and his eye were green.

933
00:32:13,132 --> 00:32:14,633
No, he really was beautiful.

934
00:32:14,633 --> 00:32:16,568
- [Crow] There was this
thing one time, I saw it.

935
00:32:16,568 --> 00:32:17,970
Boy, it was really neat too.

936
00:32:19,272 --> 00:32:22,275
- I never heard anybody
talk like that before.

937
00:32:22,275 --> 00:32:23,575
- Oh, I'm sorry, then I won't--

938
00:32:23,575 --> 00:32:25,043
- No, go on.

939
00:32:25,043 --> 00:32:28,480
- [Tom] I love it when you talk
about your other boyfriend.

940
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:30,048
- He was a friend.

941
00:32:30,048 --> 00:32:31,217
I mean, we were in love.

942
00:32:31,217 --> 00:32:32,718
- [Crow] Right.

943
00:32:32,718 --> 00:32:33,887
- And when it came time
for him to go to America,

944
00:32:33,887 --> 00:32:34,987
we asked if he could stay.

945
00:32:34,987 --> 00:32:35,855
- [Crow] Oh sure, sure.

946
00:32:35,855 --> 00:32:37,057
- They said no.

947
00:32:37,057 --> 00:32:38,557
And we asked if I could
go and they said no

948
00:32:38,557 --> 00:32:40,927
and finally they said he
didn't have to go at all.

949
00:32:40,927 --> 00:32:42,128
- [Crow] Uh-huh.

950
00:32:42,128 --> 00:32:43,628
- And?

951
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:45,798
- And he disappeared.

952
00:32:45,798 --> 00:32:47,033
- [Crow] Huh?

953
00:32:47,033 --> 00:32:48,200
- No one knows anything,
not even his roommate.

954
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,668
- [Mike] Let's
crack the Pringles.

955
00:32:49,668 --> 00:32:51,737
- What must be must be.

956
00:32:51,737 --> 00:32:52,905
- Don't you get tired
of hearing that?

957
00:32:52,905 --> 00:32:54,307
- [Crow] They're at EST camp.

958
00:32:56,242 --> 00:32:57,510
- [Lena] What's wrong?

959
00:32:57,510 --> 00:32:59,145
- I've never heard
anyone say that.

960
00:32:59,145 --> 00:33:00,913
I mean, I've thought of that.

961
00:33:00,913 --> 00:33:02,115
- [Tom] I think.

962
00:33:02,115 --> 00:33:03,448
- But I've never
heard anyone say it.

963
00:33:03,448 --> 00:33:06,318
Everyone here believes
what must be must be.

964
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:07,587
- Richard, stop!

965
00:33:07,587 --> 00:33:10,122
We're not supposed to
be talking like that.

966
00:33:10,122 --> 00:33:12,292
- Why? There's nobody
within miles of us.

967
00:33:12,292 --> 00:33:14,127
- [Mike] I used "agree" today.

968
00:33:14,127 --> 00:33:15,828
- You know, you're right.

969
00:33:15,828 --> 00:33:17,063
(Tom chuckling)

970
00:33:17,063 --> 00:33:18,130
- You know, Lena?

971
00:33:18,130 --> 00:33:19,065
- What?

972
00:33:19,065 --> 00:33:20,265
- I love it when you laugh.

973
00:33:20,265 --> 00:33:21,700
- [Crow] Boy, if
only you had a nose.

974
00:33:22,568 --> 00:33:23,402
- I like you.

975
00:33:23,402 --> 00:33:25,270
- [Tom] You have skin.

976
00:33:25,270 --> 00:33:27,607
(pleasant music)

977
00:33:27,607 --> 00:33:29,675
- I like you a lot.

978
00:33:29,675 --> 00:33:31,743
- [Mike] Look at that, he
has really feminine hands.

979
00:33:31,743 --> 00:33:33,713
(Crow laughing)

980
00:33:33,713 --> 00:33:36,615
- [Crow] Shouldn't we wrestle
and slap each other now?

981
00:33:36,615 --> 00:33:39,218
(upbeat music)

982
00:33:44,690 --> 00:33:46,692
- [Mike] I guess I gotta go
a little easier next time.

983
00:33:46,692 --> 00:33:48,227
- You know, right
before I met you,

984
00:33:48,227 --> 00:33:51,797
I found a piece of metal
and it had a word on it.

985
00:33:51,797 --> 00:33:54,500
- [Tom] Only you can
prevent groin fires.

986
00:33:54,500 --> 00:33:55,668
- "Milwaukee."

987
00:33:56,935 --> 00:33:59,105
And I asked...
- Wow.

988
00:33:59,105 --> 00:34:01,673
- If it came from
America and they said no.

989
00:34:01,673 --> 00:34:02,908
- [Crow] Hmmm.

990
00:34:02,908 --> 00:34:04,043
- And then I asked
the confessional

991
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,780
and it said it was a
plant from the ocean.

992
00:34:07,780 --> 00:34:10,248
- [Crow] She really was
on top of Ol' Smokey, huh?

993
00:34:10,248 --> 00:34:11,517
(Tom chuckling)

994
00:34:11,517 --> 00:34:13,018
- You know, when I
was a little girl

995
00:34:13,018 --> 00:34:15,053
and I lived in the north
section, I saw something.

996
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:16,522
- [Mike] Wow, that's amazing.

997
00:34:17,390 --> 00:34:19,325
- One day, I was out playing

998
00:34:19,325 --> 00:34:21,027
and I saw one of the guide cars.

999
00:34:21,027 --> 00:34:22,528
- [Tom] Really?

1000
00:34:22,528 --> 00:34:23,462
- And there was something
there that was covered,

1001
00:34:23,462 --> 00:34:26,132
so I was curious and a peeked.

1002
00:34:26,132 --> 00:34:27,400
- [Richard] And?

1003
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:28,567
- [Tom] She looks like
Henry Silva in a wig.

1004
00:34:28,567 --> 00:34:30,770
- I saw one of the
older members, Richard.

1005
00:34:30,770 --> 00:34:32,003
He was very still.

1006
00:34:32,003 --> 00:34:34,173
- [Mike] She fell asleep
on dermabrasion wheel.

1007
00:34:34,173 --> 00:34:35,475
- [Crow] Ow.

1008
00:34:35,475 --> 00:34:36,575
- And they said he was asleep,

1009
00:34:36,575 --> 00:34:39,012
that sleep was very important.

1010
00:34:39,012 --> 00:34:40,913
But I'll never forget
how odd it looked.

1011
00:34:40,913 --> 00:34:42,315
- [Tom] Do you like paper?

1012
00:34:42,315 --> 00:34:43,548
- We've gotta find out more.

1013
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:45,050
- No.

1014
00:34:45,050 --> 00:34:46,485
I'm frightened.

1015
00:34:46,485 --> 00:34:48,020
- I am too.

1016
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:49,555
But something's not right.

1017
00:34:50,957 --> 00:34:53,158
Unanswered questions,
Lena, have to be answered.

1018
00:34:53,158 --> 00:34:55,862
- Richard, no, please.

1019
00:34:55,862 --> 00:34:57,930
I am frightened, you
don't understand that.

1020
00:34:57,930 --> 00:34:59,398
- It'll be okay.

1021
00:34:59,398 --> 00:35:00,767
- [Mike] Come on, let's put
out our flaming crotches

1022
00:35:00,767 --> 00:35:01,833
and we'll find your nose.

1023
00:35:01,833 --> 00:35:02,668
- Hey.

1024
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:04,437
Trust me.

1025
00:35:04,437 --> 00:35:05,672
- [Crow] After all,

1026
00:35:05,672 --> 00:35:07,005
I look like the guy
on "Three's Company."

1027
00:35:07,005 --> 00:35:08,273
- [Richard] Okay?

1028
00:35:08,273 --> 00:35:10,810
- [Mike] Is your face
made out of clay or...

1029
00:35:10,810 --> 00:35:12,345
- Okay.

1030
00:35:12,345 --> 00:35:14,880
- [Tom] Now let's help Jack
and Krissy move that couch.

1031
00:35:15,882 --> 00:35:17,048
(gunshot booming)
- Ow!

1032
00:35:18,217 --> 00:35:22,755
(Mike, Crow and Tom
huffing and groaning)

1033
00:35:24,123 --> 00:35:25,858
- [Mike] Des Moines Olympics
are kind of a letdown,

1034
00:35:25,858 --> 00:35:27,293
aren't they?

1035
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:28,760
- Richard.

1036
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:30,295
Are you okay?

1037
00:35:30,295 --> 00:35:31,230
- I'm fine.

1038
00:35:31,230 --> 00:35:32,165
- [Crow] I'm just a puss.

1039
00:35:32,165 --> 00:35:33,532
- I see, well you slowed down.

1040
00:35:33,532 --> 00:35:35,568
I thought maybe it was
your ankle or something.

1041
00:35:35,568 --> 00:35:37,603
- No, I just slowed down.

1042
00:35:37,603 --> 00:35:38,570
- I don't understand.

1043
00:35:38,570 --> 00:35:40,640
You can't just slow down.

1044
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:42,542
When you're in a
race you have to win.

1045
00:35:43,708 --> 00:35:44,843
- Why?

1046
00:35:44,843 --> 00:35:46,312
- Why?

1047
00:35:46,312 --> 00:35:47,547
What kind of a question is that?

1048
00:35:47,547 --> 00:35:49,148
- [Tom] I'm just your
Time Life operator.

1049
00:35:49,148 --> 00:35:50,983
- Why get involved
in a race at all

1050
00:35:50,983 --> 00:35:52,218
if you're not gonna
give it all you've got?

1051
00:35:52,218 --> 00:35:53,953
- [Mike] Was this an
after school special?

1052
00:35:53,953 --> 00:35:55,722
- I gave it all
I wanted to give.

1053
00:35:55,722 --> 00:35:57,323
I just didn't feel like winning.

1054
00:35:58,190 --> 00:35:59,958
- I'll have to report this.

1055
00:35:59,958 --> 00:36:01,093
- To who?

1056
00:36:01,093 --> 00:36:02,495
- [Crow] To the council
of loser clones.

1057
00:36:02,495 --> 00:36:03,728
- I'll have to report that too.

1058
00:36:03,728 --> 00:36:06,398
- [Tom] It's
starting to stack up.

1059
00:36:06,398 --> 00:36:08,033
- Can I go now?

1060
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:09,468
- Sure you can go.

1061
00:36:09,468 --> 00:36:11,170
- [Mike] Yeah, report my ass.

1062
00:36:11,170 --> 00:36:13,638
- [Tom] This is one of the
12 Steve Prefontaine movies

1063
00:36:13,638 --> 00:36:15,307
being released this year.

1064
00:36:15,307 --> 00:36:16,142
It's great.

1065
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:18,978
- [Mike] "Crotch Fires and You."

1066
00:36:20,445 --> 00:36:23,382
- [Tom] Let's see, "Jake
Cardigan pulled his hovercraft."

1067
00:36:24,483 --> 00:36:27,152
(ominous music)

1068
00:36:28,653 --> 00:36:31,557
- [Mike] Did I finish
those cheese curls?

1069
00:36:31,557 --> 00:36:33,292
- [Tom] Doo, doo, doo.

1070
00:36:33,292 --> 00:36:34,860
(gasping)

1071
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:36,328
- [Crow] I'm coming, Elizabeth.

1072
00:36:36,328 --> 00:36:37,263
I'm coming.

1073
00:36:37,263 --> 00:36:38,830
Elizabeth, I'm coming.

1074
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:40,065
- [Mike] Feels like
an elephant clone

1075
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:42,235
is sitting on my chest.

1076
00:36:42,235 --> 00:36:44,237
- [Tom] The James Garner Story.

1077
00:36:45,270 --> 00:36:46,105
- [Crow] Beef.

1078
00:36:46,105 --> 00:36:48,307
It's what's for dinner.

1079
00:36:48,307 --> 00:36:49,808
Oh.

1080
00:36:49,808 --> 00:36:53,078
- [Mike] Hi, we're your
heart attack consultants.

1081
00:36:53,078 --> 00:36:55,915
- [Tom] Let's get you out
on that track, young man.

1082
00:36:55,915 --> 00:36:57,383
- [Mike] Oh, please be careful.

1083
00:36:57,383 --> 00:36:59,418
My chalky, spongy midsection.

1084
00:36:59,418 --> 00:37:02,087
(ominous music)

1085
00:37:02,087 --> 00:37:04,723
- [Crow] On Tuesdays you
get extra prints for free!

1086
00:37:04,723 --> 00:37:07,393
- [Tom] God, the
human body is hideous.

1087
00:37:07,393 --> 00:37:08,327
- Huh.

1088
00:37:08,327 --> 00:37:10,428
Well, I can't see anything.

1089
00:37:10,428 --> 00:37:11,863
- [Mike] You're dull
and lumpy inside too.

1090
00:37:11,863 --> 00:37:13,765
- What did it feel like?

1091
00:37:13,765 --> 00:37:17,837
- It felt like a burning
sensation in my chest.

1092
00:37:17,837 --> 00:37:19,338
- [Crow] Well, Richard,

1093
00:37:19,338 --> 00:37:20,673
did you makes a run for
the boarder earlier today?

1094
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:23,008
- Are you sleeping okay?

1095
00:37:23,008 --> 00:37:24,843
- Sure, fine.

1096
00:37:24,843 --> 00:37:26,945
It just happened so quick,
I don't know what it is.

1097
00:37:26,945 --> 00:37:28,713
- [Tom] Have you been
eating your boogers?

1098
00:37:28,713 --> 00:37:30,617
- Let me ask you, Richard?

1099
00:37:30,617 --> 00:37:31,817
Do you spend a lot of
time in the country?

1100
00:37:31,817 --> 00:37:33,818
- Or down by the river?

1101
00:37:34,820 --> 00:37:36,122
- No.

1102
00:37:36,122 --> 00:37:36,955
Why?

1103
00:37:36,955 --> 00:37:38,190
- Oh, no reason.

1104
00:37:38,190 --> 00:37:39,358
It's just that the
air by the river

1105
00:37:39,358 --> 00:37:40,760
is not really very good for you.

1106
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:41,693
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

1107
00:37:41,693 --> 00:37:42,628
- We just thought that it might

1108
00:37:42,628 --> 00:37:43,428
have something to do with it.

1109
00:37:43,428 --> 00:37:44,363
- [Mike] Am I dead?

1110
00:37:44,363 --> 00:37:45,865
- What do you think it is?

1111
00:37:45,865 --> 00:37:47,967
- Oh, just a little attack
of the nerves, I guess.

1112
00:37:47,967 --> 00:37:50,837
After all, you're probably
excited about going to America.

1113
00:37:50,837 --> 00:37:52,305
- [Tom] Today!

1114
00:37:52,305 --> 00:37:53,872
- Yes.

1115
00:37:53,872 --> 00:37:55,140
You're scheduled
to go in two days.

1116
00:37:55,140 --> 00:37:56,642
- [Crow] We traded
you to Cincinnati.

1117
00:37:56,642 --> 00:38:00,378
- We were going to wait but
you've been progressing so well,

1118
00:38:00,378 --> 00:38:02,147
we're letting you go early.

1119
00:38:02,147 --> 00:38:03,615
- Jeez.
- Isn't that nice?

1120
00:38:03,615 --> 00:38:04,817
- [Mike] Ugh.

1121
00:38:04,817 --> 00:38:06,352
- Great.

1122
00:38:06,352 --> 00:38:08,820
- So why don't you go and
get some sleep, all right?

1123
00:38:08,820 --> 00:38:11,023
Take these pills just
before you go to bed,

1124
00:38:11,023 --> 00:38:12,425
I'm sure you're not going
to have any trouble at all.

1125
00:38:12,425 --> 00:38:14,827
- [Mike] Can I bring
my bike to America?

1126
00:38:14,827 --> 00:38:15,662
- Okay.

1127
00:38:17,997 --> 00:38:18,930
- [Tom] Nice gal.

1128
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:24,170
- Well, did you hear enough?

1129
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:25,403
- He's lying.

1130
00:38:25,403 --> 00:38:26,905
- [Crow] He looks
like an adult fetus.

1131
00:38:28,207 --> 00:38:29,675
- [Mike] They found my nose!

1132
00:38:29,675 --> 00:38:31,910
- [Tom] The tight short
clinic has been so much fun!

1133
00:38:31,910 --> 00:38:33,912
- I'm so happy to see you.

1134
00:38:33,912 --> 00:38:36,915
- [Crow] Allan and I are getting
married, isn't that great?!

1135
00:38:38,650 --> 00:38:40,052
- Lena, we're being watched.

1136
00:38:40,052 --> 00:38:41,553
- Richard, what're
you talking about?

1137
00:38:41,553 --> 00:38:42,955
- I tried a test last night.

1138
00:38:42,955 --> 00:38:45,590
I pretended I was sick
when no one was around.

1139
00:38:45,590 --> 00:38:47,025
We are being watched.

1140
00:38:47,025 --> 00:38:48,093
- Richard, why
would they watch us?

1141
00:38:48,093 --> 00:38:49,962
For what reason?

1142
00:38:49,962 --> 00:38:51,463
- [Richard] I don't know.

1143
00:38:51,463 --> 00:38:53,765
- [Mike] Maybe to see if
we do that rubbing thing.

1144
00:38:53,765 --> 00:38:57,235
- [Tom] Let's go pray at the
shrine of Dolly the sheep.

1145
00:38:57,235 --> 00:38:59,238
(wind howling)

1146
00:38:59,238 --> 00:39:01,540
- [Crow] Are you going
to Bobby's America party?

1147
00:39:01,540 --> 00:39:03,408
- Lena, there's something
strange happening here

1148
00:39:03,408 --> 00:39:05,077
that we're not
allowed to know about.

1149
00:39:05,077 --> 00:39:06,245
- I know.

1150
00:39:06,245 --> 00:39:07,513
Richard, ever since
you and I met,

1151
00:39:07,513 --> 00:39:09,448
the guides look at me strangely.

1152
00:39:09,448 --> 00:39:12,685
- Did you see the way they
looked at us when we first met?

1153
00:39:12,685 --> 00:39:13,518
They got angry.

1154
00:39:14,487 --> 00:39:15,955
- Speak to the confessional.

1155
00:39:15,955 --> 00:39:19,058
- I don't get any answers
from the confessional.

1156
00:39:19,058 --> 00:39:21,027
I think the only place
I'm gonna find any answers

1157
00:39:21,027 --> 00:39:21,827
is America.

1158
00:39:21,827 --> 00:39:23,062
- [Crow] Today!

1159
00:39:23,062 --> 00:39:24,163
- And I'm gonna try
and get there tonight.

1160
00:39:24,163 --> 00:39:25,297
- [Crow] Or today!

1161
00:39:25,297 --> 00:39:27,098
- But Richard,
you're not qualified.

1162
00:39:27,098 --> 00:39:28,367
- Look, I saw the guides.

1163
00:39:28,367 --> 00:39:30,702
They took George up to
the building in the hill

1164
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:32,070
after his party.

1165
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:34,140
I think that's a
good place to start.

1166
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:35,373
I'm gonna try and get in.

1167
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:36,908
- [Tom] If my SATs
are good enough.

1168
00:39:38,543 --> 00:39:39,478
- No.

1169
00:39:39,478 --> 00:39:40,947
- [Crow] You and your big nose!

1170
00:39:42,948 --> 00:39:45,617
- [Mike] So you wanna take
your shirt off now or...

1171
00:39:47,318 --> 00:39:49,188
- Lena, I have to go.

1172
00:39:49,188 --> 00:39:50,355
I've got to find out.

1173
00:39:51,657 --> 00:39:53,358
Don't be frightened.

1174
00:39:53,358 --> 00:39:55,427
- I am frightened, Richard.

1175
00:39:55,427 --> 00:39:56,762
I'm very frightened.

1176
00:39:57,830 --> 00:39:59,765
I'm never gonna see you again.

1177
00:39:59,765 --> 00:40:01,967
- Of course you're
gonna see me again.

1178
00:40:01,967 --> 00:40:03,902
I'm gonna go to America,
find out the answers

1179
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:04,803
and I'm gonna come back.

1180
00:40:04,803 --> 00:40:06,038
- Richard, why?

1181
00:40:06,038 --> 00:40:07,272
Why do you have
to go to America?

1182
00:40:07,272 --> 00:40:08,507
- [Tom] Today!

1183
00:40:08,507 --> 00:40:10,208
- Because I have to find
out for you and for me

1184
00:40:10,208 --> 00:40:11,443
and for everyone else.

1185
00:40:11,443 --> 00:40:13,312
- [Crow] For the
baby I'm carrying.

1186
00:40:13,312 --> 00:40:15,380
- Lena, you can't say
anything to anybody.

1187
00:40:15,380 --> 00:40:17,048
- [Tom] I'll leave you a
lump of dough with hair on it

1188
00:40:17,048 --> 00:40:18,383
to remind you of me.

1189
00:40:18,383 --> 00:40:20,752
(dramatic music)
- Lena.

1190
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,955
- [Mike] She's trying to
start his crotch on fire

1191
00:40:22,955 --> 00:40:23,822
with her mind.

1192
00:40:26,392 --> 00:40:29,128
- [Crow] Whoa, there
at Chuck Berry's ranch.

1193
00:40:29,128 --> 00:40:30,830
- [Tom] Aren't
these stables phony?

1194
00:40:30,830 --> 00:40:33,898
(electrical buzzing)

1195
00:40:36,435 --> 00:40:39,205
- [Crow] Yeah, Secretariat
is a personal friend of mine.

1196
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:44,610
(upbeat music)

1197
00:40:48,647 --> 00:40:50,215
(singing tune)

1198
00:40:50,215 --> 00:40:51,850
- Ah, red!

1199
00:40:51,850 --> 00:40:53,485
- Hey, that was blue, I saw.

1200
00:40:53,485 --> 00:40:54,453
- No it wasn't.

1201
00:40:54,453 --> 00:40:55,620
- You're in the molasses swamp.

1202
00:40:55,620 --> 00:40:56,588
- I am not.

1203
00:40:56,588 --> 00:40:57,957
- Yeah, he's in molasses swamp.

1204
00:40:57,957 --> 00:40:59,858
- [Both] You're
in molasses swamp!

1205
00:40:59,858 --> 00:41:01,027
You're in molasses swamp!

1206
00:41:01,027 --> 00:41:02,595
You're in molasses swamp!

1207
00:41:02,595 --> 00:41:03,728
- Mike...
- You're in molasses swamp!

1208
00:41:03,728 --> 00:41:05,130
- You know me.

1209
00:41:05,130 --> 00:41:06,265
I'm a patient woman.
- You're in molasses swamp!

1210
00:41:06,265 --> 00:41:07,098
- Shut up!

1211
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:11,770
Oh, momma, do I need a break.

1212
00:41:11,770 --> 00:41:15,707
I sure could use that old
electronic babysitter right now.

1213
00:41:15,707 --> 00:41:19,010
So could you guys quick
whip up a TV show,

1214
00:41:19,010 --> 00:41:21,013
maybe one of them
public kid shows.

1215
00:41:21,013 --> 00:41:22,280
You know, educational.

1216
00:41:22,280 --> 00:41:25,350
You know the kind of
crap I'm talking about.

1217
00:41:25,350 --> 00:41:26,752
(Bobo groaning)

1218
00:41:26,752 --> 00:41:27,887
(laughing)

1219
00:41:27,887 --> 00:41:30,588
- Ah, Mrs. Forrester,
so you need me

1220
00:41:30,588 --> 00:41:33,358
and I have all the power.
(laughing)

1221
00:41:33,358 --> 00:41:35,928
Once again you see there
is nothing you can possess

1222
00:41:35,928 --> 00:41:38,030
which I cannot take away.

1223
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,063
Too bad.

1224
00:41:39,063 --> 00:41:41,067
The Havidos could've warned you

1225
00:41:41,067 --> 00:41:42,802
if only you spoke Havidos.

1226
00:41:42,802 --> 00:41:45,370
(speaking foreign language)

1227
00:41:45,370 --> 00:41:46,338
- Ugh.

1228
00:41:46,338 --> 00:41:49,208
Oh, would you just help me out.

1229
00:41:49,208 --> 00:41:52,310
Hey, kids, "Satellite
of Love" is on.

1230
00:41:52,310 --> 00:41:55,147
- Oh, I don't like
that show, it's dumb.

1231
00:41:55,147 --> 00:41:56,715
- It's got robots.

1232
00:41:56,715 --> 00:41:59,252
- Robots are dumb, you're dumb.

1233
00:41:59,252 --> 00:42:01,853
- I took the liberty of
making some fruit leather.

1234
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:02,888
- What the hell is--

1235
00:42:02,888 --> 00:42:04,857
- [Kids] Fruit leather!

1236
00:42:04,857 --> 00:42:06,058
(chiming music)

1237
00:42:06,058 --> 00:42:10,228
♪ We'll have fun on
the Satellite of Love ♪

1238
00:42:10,228 --> 00:42:11,063
♪ Today ♪

1239
00:42:11,063 --> 00:42:13,932
(giggling)

1240
00:42:13,932 --> 00:42:15,400
- Hi, kids!
- Hi.

1241
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:17,803
- I'm Crow the...

1242
00:42:17,803 --> 00:42:19,037
Cow.
(laughing)

1243
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:22,307
And this is Tommy the
timid tuna, right.

1244
00:42:22,307 --> 00:42:23,142
- Aaaww.

1245
00:42:23,142 --> 00:42:24,577
- Today's letter...

1246
00:42:27,780 --> 00:42:28,613
- A.

1247
00:42:29,915 --> 00:42:30,748
- A?

1248
00:42:32,250 --> 00:42:33,885
- [Both] A!

1249
00:42:33,885 --> 00:42:35,820
(laughing)

1250
00:42:35,820 --> 00:42:38,490
(clearing throat)

1251
00:42:38,490 --> 00:42:40,192
- Today's number.

1252
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:43,595
- Three.

1253
00:42:43,595 --> 00:42:44,430
(gasping)

1254
00:42:44,430 --> 00:42:45,630
- Three?

1255
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:47,633
(laughing)

1256
00:42:47,633 --> 00:42:48,800
So today...

1257
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:50,535
Today we learned...

1258
00:42:50,535 --> 00:42:52,037
- A

1259
00:42:52,037 --> 00:42:53,972
and three.

1260
00:42:53,972 --> 00:42:55,573
♪ Today we learned ♪

1261
00:42:55,573 --> 00:42:57,175
♪ A and three ♪

1262
00:42:57,175 --> 00:42:59,512
♪ Today we learned A and three ♪

1263
00:42:59,512 --> 00:43:01,147
(laughing)

1264
00:43:01,147 --> 00:43:03,348
