2498
01:26:12,568 --> 01:26:13,703
- [Mike] Arrrr.

2499
01:26:13,703 --> 01:26:14,937
- Ladies and gentlemen
of the press,

2500
01:26:14,937 --> 01:26:16,438
let's get right
to the questions.

2501
01:26:16,438 --> 01:26:18,240
- [Tom] Who's coming up
this week on "Biography?"

2502
01:26:18,240 --> 01:26:19,108
- Miss Grady.

2503
01:26:19,108 --> 01:26:20,042
- [Crow] Grady!

2504
01:26:20,042 --> 01:26:21,543
- [Grady] Senator Knight,

2505
01:26:21,543 --> 01:26:24,047
what will your position be on
the subject of human rights?

2506
01:26:24,047 --> 01:26:26,082
- [Jeff] Well, you know, I
talked a great deal about that

2507
01:26:26,082 --> 01:26:27,950
during the campaign but
I think it's important

2508
01:26:27,950 --> 01:26:29,052
to repeat it now.

2509
01:26:29,052 --> 01:26:30,987
As president, my
position will be

2510
01:26:30,987 --> 01:26:33,557
that any suppression of
rights or infringement--

2511
01:26:33,557 --> 01:26:34,657
- [Mike] Wow.

2512
01:26:34,657 --> 01:26:35,725
- [Crow] Mm-hmm.

2513
01:26:35,725 --> 01:26:37,093
- [Mike] Get it?!

2514
01:26:37,093 --> 01:26:38,327
(Tom giggling)

2515
01:26:38,327 --> 01:26:40,297
- As such cannot and
will not be tolerated.

2516
01:26:40,297 --> 01:26:41,863
- [Crow] Senator, I'm
Brown from the Sun.

2517
01:26:41,863 --> 01:26:42,998
- Senator!

2518
01:26:42,998 --> 01:26:44,367
- [Jeff] Yes,
gentleman in the back.

2519
01:26:44,367 --> 01:26:45,468
- Bernie, Daily Sun.

2520
01:26:45,468 --> 01:26:46,937
- [Tom] I love Bridget.

2521
01:26:46,937 --> 01:26:48,705
- Senator could you please
tell us about Clonus.

2522
01:26:50,607 --> 01:26:52,242
- [Mike] Arrrr?

2523
01:26:52,242 --> 01:26:53,242
- [Crow] Yes, definitely.

2524
01:26:53,242 --> 01:26:54,477
Um, Brit Hume, front row.

2525
01:26:56,778 --> 01:26:58,948
- [Tom] I can barely
hear my heart beating.

2526
01:27:00,517 --> 01:27:02,585
- [Mike] I'm a sad clown.

2527
01:27:02,585 --> 01:27:05,120
- [Crow] Boy, that clock
never moves, does it?

2528
01:27:05,120 --> 01:27:06,688
(ominous music)

2529
01:27:06,688 --> 01:27:07,623
- [Tom] Was that a bad movie

2530
01:27:07,623 --> 01:27:09,058
or was I just in the wrong mood?

2531
01:27:09,058 --> 01:27:10,760
- [Crow] Oh, we can
leave, all right!

2532
01:27:10,760 --> 01:27:11,593
- [Mike] Wait...

2533
01:27:11,593 --> 01:27:13,062
Oh.

2534
01:27:13,062 --> 01:27:14,263
Oh boy.

2535
01:27:14,263 --> 01:27:15,865
Executive producer,
Walter Fiveson,

2536
01:27:15,865 --> 01:27:18,500
was a good friend of
Supervising Executive Producer

2537
01:27:18,500 --> 01:27:19,635
Ray Dryden.

2538
01:27:19,635 --> 01:27:20,903
They grew up together
in a log cabin

2539
01:27:20,903 --> 01:27:24,440
with a woman involved in
casting, Susan Arnold.

2540
01:27:24,440 --> 01:27:27,077
- [Tom] But all was
not as it seemed.

2541
01:27:27,077 --> 01:27:29,278
- [Crow] The arrival
of Associate Producer

2542
01:27:29,278 --> 01:27:32,715
Peter R.J. Deyell, proved
both groundbreaking

2543
01:27:32,715 --> 01:27:36,018
and heart wrenching for
the young Liverpoolians.

2544
01:27:36,018 --> 01:27:38,420
- [Mike] And then
Co-Producer Michael Lee

2545
01:27:38,420 --> 01:27:41,323
and Carolyn Haber and Michael
Lee and Paul Berkowitz

2546
01:27:41,323 --> 01:27:43,358
and Joe Gianonne
and Robert Cummings

2547
01:27:43,358 --> 01:27:45,828
and Michael Lacoe
and some other guys

2548
01:27:45,828 --> 01:27:46,895
and Harley Pence.

2549
01:27:46,895 --> 01:27:48,130
- [Tom] I'll take it, Mike.

2550
01:27:48,130 --> 01:27:50,265
The oddly named,
Timaree McCormick,

2551
01:27:50,265 --> 01:27:51,933
young and brilliant
production assistant,

2552
01:27:51,933 --> 01:27:54,970
developed an unhealthy
fixation of Joe Blasco,

2553
01:27:54,970 --> 01:27:57,173
founder of the Joe
Blasco Makeup School.

2554
01:27:57,173 --> 01:27:58,708
- [Crow] I'll take it.

2555
01:27:58,708 --> 01:28:01,343
Dwight LaVers, a name known to
millions, yet a dark mystery,

2556
01:28:01,343 --> 01:28:03,980
to even his closest friends.

2557
01:28:03,980 --> 01:28:05,748
- [Mike] Tomorrow,
the fascinating world

2558
01:28:05,748 --> 01:28:08,918
of M.A "Ma" Schreibman who
conquered his blindness

2559
01:28:08,918 --> 01:28:11,553
to become one of the most
sought after visual consultants

2560
01:28:11,553 --> 01:28:12,988
in the business.

2561
01:28:12,988 --> 01:28:14,790
- [Tom] The thin stylings
of Brogan DePard...

2562
01:28:14,790 --> 01:28:16,258
Brogan...

2563
01:28:16,258 --> 01:28:18,493
Paul Sharp and Ted Keep,
two crisply-named young men,

2564
01:28:18,493 --> 01:28:19,995
tonight on "Biography."

2565
01:28:21,130 --> 01:28:23,700
- [Crow] Freeze Frame,
the J. Geils Band.

2566
01:28:23,700 --> 01:28:26,135
Synonyms in the hearts
of Americans everywhere.

2567
01:28:26,135 --> 01:28:28,370
(Mike laughing)

2568
01:28:28,370 --> 01:28:29,572
- [Mike] Ah!

2569
01:28:29,572 --> 01:28:31,773
Peter Graves, the
underrated, underpaid

2570
01:28:31,773 --> 01:28:33,777
and incredibly handsome
host of "Biography,"

2571
01:28:33,777 --> 01:28:35,378
tonight on "Biography."

2572
01:28:35,378 --> 01:28:37,080
- [Crow] Tonight on "Biography,"

2573
01:28:37,080 --> 01:28:39,848
Paulette Breen who turned
down perfectly innocent

2574
01:28:39,848 --> 01:28:41,850
sexually advances
from Peter Graves

2575
01:28:41,850 --> 01:28:43,518
on the set of the
movie "Clonus,"

2576
01:28:43,518 --> 01:28:45,688
who will never work
in this town again.

2577
01:28:45,688 --> 01:28:47,857
- [Tom] James Mantell, in
a striking coincidence,

2578
01:28:47,857 --> 01:28:50,258
shared a first name with
the hulking, expressionless

2579
01:28:50,258 --> 01:28:52,462
pseudo cowboy, James Arness.

2580
01:28:52,462 --> 01:28:53,963
James Arness,

2581
01:28:53,963 --> 01:28:56,932
as a young boy, James Arness
nurtured a howling bitterness

2582
01:28:56,932 --> 01:28:59,368
in the face of the
awesomely superior talent

2583
01:28:59,368 --> 01:29:01,270
of his brother, Peter Graves.

2584
01:29:01,270 --> 01:29:03,272
Peter Graves' life
and career were marked

2585
01:29:03,272 --> 01:29:06,042
by a generosity of spirit
and loving attitude

2586
01:29:06,042 --> 01:29:08,310
towards his fell man, which
were altogether missing

2587
01:29:08,310 --> 01:29:11,047
in the pitted soul
if James Arness.

2588
01:29:11,047 --> 01:29:13,983
Often, James Arness' mother
would remark to friends

2589
01:29:13,983 --> 01:29:17,587
that she loved her son, Peter
Graves, so very, very much,

2590
01:29:17,587 --> 01:29:20,022
while she hates James
Arness and cursed the day

2591
01:29:20,022 --> 01:29:22,525
her womb had been blighted
with such a creature.

2592
01:29:22,525 --> 01:29:24,927
James Arness, ugly and stupid.

2593
01:29:24,927 --> 01:29:26,562
Tonight on "Biography."

2594
01:29:27,863 --> 01:29:29,098
- [Crow] Okay.

2595
01:29:29,098 --> 01:29:30,265
- [Mike] That's as
good as it gets.

2596
01:29:30,265 --> 01:29:32,168
So, Peter Graves?
- Biography.

2597
01:29:32,168 --> 01:29:33,502
- [Mike] Biography.

2598
01:29:33,502 --> 01:29:34,903
- Agua!

2599
01:29:34,903 --> 01:29:36,705
(rumbling)

2600
01:29:36,705 --> 01:29:38,573
(thudding)

2601
01:29:38,573 --> 01:29:40,710
(beeping)

2602
01:29:40,710 --> 01:29:42,512
(mechanical buzzing)

2603
01:29:42,512 --> 01:29:44,580
(chains rattling)

2604
01:29:44,580 --> 01:29:47,317
(buzzing)

2605
01:29:47,317 --> 01:29:49,752
(clearing throat)

2606
01:29:49,752 --> 01:29:52,522
So, what do you think
of my new nose job?

2607
01:29:52,522 --> 01:29:54,590
- It's downright
Bruce Jennerian.

2608
01:29:54,590 --> 01:29:57,093
- Yes, well I went a little
deeper than I might have

2609
01:29:57,093 --> 01:30:00,295
because I feel I can always
add more later if I wanted.

2610
01:30:01,130 --> 01:30:02,932
- Mike, Bobo's calling.

2611
01:30:02,932 --> 01:30:05,233
- What're you looking at?

2612
01:30:05,233 --> 01:30:07,770
- Please, Mike, keep it quiet.

2613
01:30:07,770 --> 01:30:10,038
Evil orphan space
children were very fussy

2614
01:30:10,038 --> 01:30:11,307
getting down tonight.

2615
01:30:11,307 --> 01:30:14,043
I think they're
off their routine.

2616
01:30:14,043 --> 01:30:16,645
- Aw, well I've
got just the thing.

2617
01:30:16,645 --> 01:30:17,913
I wrote a little night music

2618
01:30:17,913 --> 01:30:20,015
inspired by a poem
I've always loved.

2619
01:30:20,015 --> 01:30:24,287
The words are, "Sleep,
oh fair one, sleep.

2620
01:30:24,287 --> 01:30:26,155
"The night is low and drowsy,

2621
01:30:26,155 --> 01:30:28,958
"your dreams are fair and deep.

2622
01:30:28,958 --> 01:30:32,995
"On feeble tender wings
rest all Earthly things.

2623
01:30:32,995 --> 01:30:35,097
"Sleep, oh gentle lamb,

2624
01:30:35,097 --> 01:30:38,167
"till morning mother
sun does bring."

2625
01:30:38,167 --> 01:30:39,835
- That's beautiful.

2626
01:30:39,835 --> 01:30:40,637
- Okay, Mike.

2627
01:30:42,972 --> 01:30:46,875
(exciting marching band music)

2628
01:30:48,643 --> 01:30:50,480
(crying)

2629
01:30:50,480 --> 01:30:52,282
- You are so dead, Nelson!

2630
01:30:52,282 --> 01:30:55,183
It is a John Agar
film festival for you!

2631
01:30:56,185 --> 01:30:57,687
(thudding)
(groaning)

2632
01:30:57,687 --> 01:30:59,655
(crying)

2633
01:30:59,655 --> 01:31:02,123
(somber music)

2634
01:32:00,515 --> 01:32:01,350
- Sure.

